  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **`setup_relative::transform_between(world, from, to) -> Result<Location, String>`** (new `crates/app/src/setup_relative.rs`): the rigid transform that takes the part as setup `from` holds it to where setup `to` holds it, `T = A_to * A_from^-1`, derived from the two setups' #326 part alignments. It is the identity for a setup and itself, composes (A->C = (B->C)(A->B)) and inverts. It refuses by name a missing setup, a name that is not a setup, and a stored alignment that is not finite or not a unit rotation; it never falls back to the identity. #317 and #318 will read it. `carry_point` maps one point.\n- **A setup placed relative to another**: `SetupDef::relative_to: Option<String>` plus the undoable `SetSetupRelative::link(world, setup, parent, [x, y, z] degrees)` / `unlink`. The turn (\"Flip over X / Turn 90° about Z / typed angles from Setup1\") is applied to the setup's part alignment through `AlignPartToSetup`, so the stock follows the same way it does in #326. The relation shown on the page is read back from the two alignments.\n- **A change to the parent carries through**: `AlignPartToSetup` on a setup that others are linked to re-places each of them, including links of links, so each keeps its transform to its parent. Their following stocks move too, all in one undo unit. If any linked setup cannot follow (for example a cylinder stock would lie on its side), the whole change is refused and the message names that setup.\n- **Refusals**: linking a setup to itself or closing a loop is refused when the command is built. `DeleteSetup` refuses a setup that another is linked to and names the linked setup. The loader rejects a link to a missing setup, or a loop of links, as a corrupt file before writing anything to the world.\n- **Project v56**: `SetupDto::relative_to` (absent = not linked). v55 and older files load unchanged.\n- **UI**: every setup after the first gets a \"Relative to previous setup\" row on its settings page (#390): Not linked / Same as <prev> / the flip and turn presets \"from <prev>\", plus typed angles with Apply. It queues `CommandKind::SetSetupRelative`, and a refusal goes to the status line.\n\n## Design vs #326's alignment\n\nThere is no second transform. #326's per-setup `part_alignment` stays the only stored transform. #316 adds a derived setup-to-setup transform and a link, and the link only carries later edits of the parent. Decisions are in `docs/decisions/316-setup-transform.md`:\n- **Datum transfer**: does not link. Its transform is already derivable (the identity when the setup is created). A transfer is a clone, not an alias: its stock and WCS do not follow the source either.\n- **Work offset**: no transform is read from it. It is a translation in the setup frame and says where program zero is, not how the part moved. G54-G59 still come from the setup, and rotated offsets are still refused.\n- **Child edits its own alignment**: the link stays, and the relation shown is whatever the new difference is.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Flip over X about the part centre (0, 0, 10): top corner (-20, -20, 20) maps to (-20, 20, 0).\n- Quarter turn about Z: (-20, -20, 20) maps to (20, -20, 20).\n- Parent turned 90° about Z with a linked child (flip) and grandchild (turn): `carried_count() == 2`, both relative transforms are unchanged, and a single undo restores all three.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/setup_relative.rs` (new, 8 tests):\n- `transform_between_reads_identity_flip_and_quarter_turn`\n- `transforms_compose_and_invert`\n- `transform_between_refuses_by_name`\n- `a_linked_setup_resolves_its_turn_into_its_alignment_and_undoes`\n- `a_change_of_the_parent_carries_into_linked_setups_in_one_undo_unit`\n- `a_linked_setup_that_cannot_follow_refuses_the_parent_change_by_name`\n- `links_refuse_self_loops_and_missing_setups_and_guard_delete`\n- `links_round_trip_and_older_or_broken_files_are_read_by_name`\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_relative_tests.rs` (2 tests):\n- `the_relative_control_links_the_setup_through_the_command`\n- `typed_turns_unlinking_and_refusals_go_through_the_drain`\n\nGate on the tree merged with current main:\n- app: setup_align, setup_mount, setups, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, golden_cl, setup_sheet, one_wcs, setup_relative\n- ui: lib, run from `crates/ui`\n- clippy `-D warnings` on app and ui (all targets)\n\nBuilds on #390 (merged).\n\nChangelog: Setups can be placed relative to the previous setup (same way up, flipped, turned, or by angles); changing that setup's part alignment carries into the linked setups; the transform between two setups is derived from their part alignments (project v56).\n\nFixes #316\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
